art of i think what's going to  show in my photography there are certain  traditions that  uphold and it kind of connects to our  ancestors  [Music]  and how long have you been working with  stained glass  35 years longer than i've been alive  we are at el matador state beach i'm  going to be meeting  ashley polsky a miniature landscape  artist  oh my goodness i feel like i'm like  nervous tonight you're like a celebrity  to me so i've been following  ashley polsky on instagram for a while  putting her artwork inside of a mint tim  you see  not only the landscape but the palette  that she used  and it's really cool to have both the  destination  and the journey i feel very connected to  you because of your  connection with medicine she is a  medical student  i am a medical doctor physician there's  the  similarity between us i can understand  the need to find something outside of  medicine that can  re-energize you ground you balance you  she is very thoughtful methodical each  brush stroke  i'm seeing her essence like i feel like  i'm witnessing a master at work  [Music]  takumi in the case of photography it's  not only about the technical mastery of  photography it's about connecting with  the person that's in the photograph  so that when you share it and people see  it they'll feel everything that you felt  in the moment when you made that  photograph  i like it how long have you been doing  it i've been blowing glass for about 14  years  i made a point of looking to find  somebody that had a message behind their  art  that's really important to me i was  diagnosed with bipolar disorder  and that's kind of makes me who i am and  feeds into  my creativity i've struggled with mental  health since i can remember  i was 13 when i was diagnosed with  clinical depression i love that he's you  know trying to bring awareness to it  it's really cool in the dark  yeah photography is my therapy it  definitely keeps me balanced  it's my time where i can just kind of  clear m